#. Not the word for English: the name of this catalog's own language, in that
#. language, as a speaker writes it in a list -- "Français", "Deutsch",
#. "Português (Brasil)". It is this language's row in the game's language
#. list, so a player who reads only this language can find it: keep its own
#. capitals. In 20 px type, on a button 472 px wide.
#. Room: at most 400 px in 20 px type; the English takes 69 px.
#: game/i18n/i18n.gd
msgid "English"
msgstr "Français"

#. The title of the settings sheet, which opens from a gear in the top-right
#. corner of every screen; also that gear's tooltip, and, in a later version,
#. a 300 px button on the launcher's first screen. One lowercase word: the
#. app's settings (here only the language, for now).
#. Room: at most 250 px in 20 px type; the English takes 77 px.
#: game/menu/corner.gd
msgid "settings"
msgstr "réglages"

#. A caption in 16 px type above the list of languages on the settings sheet.
#. One lowercase word.
#. Room: at most 472 px in 16 px type; the English takes 71 px.
#: game/menu/corner.gd
msgid "language"
msgstr "langue"

#. A button at the bottom of the settings sheet: close the sheet and go back
#. to the screen under it. One lowercase word, in 20 px type on a button 232
#. px wide.
#. Room: at most 180 px in 20 px type; the English takes 49 px.
#: game/menu/corner.gd
msgid "close"
msgstr "fermer"

#. The caption at the top of the menu of the player's worlds, in 16 px type;
#. also the tooltip of the button that opens it. A "world" is one of the three
#. the player keeps: a drop of water with everything living in it.
#. Room: at most 592 px in 16 px type; the English takes 92 px.
#: game/menu/corner.gd
msgid "your worlds"
msgstr "vos mondes"

#. The footnote under the menu of the player's worlds, in 15 px type. "Water"
#. is what everything in a world swims in; "your cell" is the player's
#. creature, which waits in the world it was left in.
#. Room: at most 592 px in 15 px type; the English takes 361 px.
#: game/menu/corner.gd
msgid "each world keeps its own water, and your cell in it"
msgstr "chaque monde garde son eau, et votre cellule dedans"

#. An empty row in the menu of the player's worlds, in 20 px type: tap it to
#. make a new world there and name it.
#. Room: at most 280 px in 20 px type; the English takes 101 px.
#: game/menu/corner.gd
msgid "new world"
msgstr "nouveau monde"

#. A small button on a world's row in the menu of the player's worlds, in 15
#. px type, 112 px wide: give the world a new name. Also the confirming button
#. of the naming sheet, in 20 px type, 232 px wide.
#. Room: at most 88 px in 15 px type; the English takes 57 px.
#: game/menu/corner.gd
msgid "rename"
msgstr "renommer"

#. A small button on a world's row, in 15 px type, 112 px wide: delete the
#. world (it asks first). Also the confirming button of that question, in 20
#. px type, 208 px wide.
#. Room: at most 88 px in 15 px type; the English takes 46 px.
#: game/menu/corner.gd
msgid "delete"
msgstr "supprimer"

#. The title of the sheet that names a new world, in 22 px type. A "world" is
#. one of the three the player keeps: a drop of water with everything living
#. in it.
#. Room: at most 512 px in 22 px type; the English takes 129 px.
#: game/menu/corner.gd
msgid "a new world"
msgstr "un nouveau monde"

#. The confirming button of the sheet that names a new world, in 20 px type,
#. 232 px wide: make the new world, with the name typed above. "It" is the
#. world.
#. Room: at most 188 px in 20 px type; the English takes 73 px.
#: game/menu/corner.gd
msgid "make it"
msgstr "le créer"

#. The title of the sheet that renames one of the player's worlds, in 22 px
#. type.
#. Room: at most 512 px in 22 px type; the English takes 194 px.
#: game/menu/corner.gd
msgid "rename this world"
msgstr "renommer ce monde"

#. A button on the naming sheet, in 20 px type, 160 px wide: go back to the
#. menu of worlds, changing nothing.
#. Room: at most 116 px in 20 px type; the English takes 46 px.
#: game/menu/corner.gd
msgid "back"
msgstr "retour"

#. The question asked before a world is deleted, in 22 px type, wrapping onto
#. two lines if it must. %s is the world's name, in the player's own words or
#. a default name such as "pond water": keep %s.
#: game/menu/corner.gd
#, c-format
msgid "delete %s?"
msgstr "supprimer %s ?"

#. Under that question, in 17 px type, wrapping: what deleting the world does.
#. A full sentence with a full stop. "It" is the world; "your cell" is the
#. player's creature, which waits in the world it was left in.
#: game/menu/corner.gd
msgid "everything living in it, and your cell with it, is gone for good."
msgstr "tout ce qui y vit, et votre cellule avec, disparaît pour de bon."

#. The caption on a button in the top-right corner, in 17 px type, before the
#. name of the world that is selected ("world pond water"). A "world" is one
#. of the three the player keeps: a drop of water and everything in it, named
#. by the player. One lowercase word.
#. Room: at most 80 px in 17 px type; the English takes 47 px.
#: game/menu/corner.gd
msgid "world"
msgstr "monde"

#. The hint along the bottom edge of the screen, in small type. It names the
#. key that goes back, and the key differs by device: `back` is the Android
#. Back button or gesture, `esc` is the Escape key. The launcher is the app's
#. main menu, the screen with the play button.
#: game/mode_select.gd
msgid "back returns to the launcher"
msgstr "retour vers le launcher"

#. The hint along the bottom edge of the screen, in small type. It names the
#. key that goes back, and the key differs by device: `back` is the Android
#. Back button or gesture, `esc` is the Escape key. The launcher is the app's
#. main menu, the screen with the play button.
#. Label "Hint" in game/mode_select.tscn
#: game/mode_select.gd game/mode_select.tscn
msgid "esc returns to the launcher"
msgstr "échap pour retourner au launcher"

#. A note in 15 px type under a button. The button is "by invite" (the way to
#. reach a friend's game by an invite they sent you), so this says who:
#. someone who is not in the same house, and who sent you an invite. Under a
#. button 320 px wide: about 40 characters at most.
#: game/mode_select.gd
msgid "a friend far away, who sent you one"
msgstr "un ami au loin, qui vous en a envoyé une"

#. Same note, for the case where the button's own name does not mention an
#. invite, so the note says how instead. About 45 characters at most.
#: game/mode_select.gd
msgid "a friend far away, by the invite they sent"
msgstr "un ami au loin, par son invitation"

#. The heading of the screen where a game is started, in 17 px type. The
#. player chooses how the water is drawn for this game: a "view".
#. Label "Heading" in game/mode_select.tscn
#: game/mode_select.tscn
msgid "choose a view"
msgstr "choisir une vue"

#. Two buttons that choose how the shared game is drawn: the first shows the
#. water the cell swims in and the membrane over it, the second shows only
#. what the cell itself can feel. Also the two options on the screen where a
#. game is started.
#. The two views, as the buttons that start a game say them. Also the start of
#. a line in the menu of the player's worlds, in 15 px type, for the cell that
#. waits in a world for that view: "point of view · fourth generation", where
#. the whole line has 280 px.
#. A button, 460 px wide in 20 px type: the view that draws the water the cell
#. swims in, and the membrane (the cell's skin, which senses) over it.
#. Button "Full" in game/mode_select.tscn
#: game/mode_select.tscn game/net/earshot.gd game/run_state.gd
msgid "full vision"
msgstr "vision complète"

#. A note in 15 px type under the "full vision" button, on one line: about 60
#. characters at most.
#. Label "FullNote" in game/mode_select.tscn
#: game/mode_select.tscn
msgid "the water the cell is swimming in, and the membrane over it"
msgstr "l'eau où nage la cellule et sa membrane"

#. The second of the two buttons above: the view that shows only what the cell
#. itself can feel.
#. The two views, as the buttons that start a game say them. Also the start of
#. a line in the menu of the player's worlds, in 15 px type, for the cell that
#. waits in a world for that view: "point of view · fourth generation", where
#. the whole line has 280 px.
#. A button, 460 px wide in 20 px type: the view that shows only what the cell
#. itself can feel, as if the player were inside it.
#. Button "Pov" in game/mode_select.tscn
#: game/mode_select.tscn game/net/earshot.gd game/run_state.gd
msgid "point of view"
msgstr "point de vue"

#. A note in 15 px type under the "point of view" button: about 40 characters
#. at most.
#. Label "PovNote" in game/mode_select.tscn
#: game/mode_select.tscn
msgid "only what the cell itself can feel"
msgstr "seulement ce que la cellule perçoit"

#. The name of this feature and the heading of its first screen: two phones on
#. the same wi-fi finding each other, near enough to hear one another. Also a
#. button on the screen before this one, and the line under the heading once
#. the two are connected.
#. The feature's name: two phones near enough to hear each other. Shown under
#. the ring while the other phone is heard.
#. Button "Net" in game/mode_select.tscn
#. Label "Heading" in game/net/earshot.tscn
#: game/mode_select.tscn game/net/earshot.gd game/net/earshot.tscn game/net/net_session.gd
msgid "within earshot"
msgstr "à portée de voix"

#. A note in 15 px type under the "within earshot" button, which is 320 px
#. wide: about 35 characters at most.
#. Label "NetNote" in game/mode_select.tscn
#: game/mode_select.tscn
msgid "a friend on the same wi-fi"
msgstr "un ami sur le même wi-fi"

#. The small grey line under the sentence on the "by invite" page while no
#. invite has been pasted yet. An invite is a one-line message that a friend
#. sends you in any chat app: you copy it, paste it into the game, and the
#. game keeps it on this device for every later visit. About 45 characters.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "you paste it once · this device keeps it"
msgstr "collez-la une fois · cet appareil la conserve"

#. Shown once the call is answered. A friend's "water" is the pond (the shared
#. game world) their server keeps; "hear" is the game's word for being
#. connected. About 35 characters.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "you can hear your friend's water"
msgstr "vous entendez l'eau de votre ami"

#. A "cell" is the player's creature. One player calls (shows a code) and the
#. other answers (taps it in). Shown in 17 px type on one line, centred on the
#. screen.
#. Room: at most 1180 px in 17 px type; the English takes 338 px.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "two cells on one wi-fi, one of them calling"
msgstr "deux cellules sur un wi-fi, l'une appelle"

#. A button: start a call, so the other phone can answer it.
#. Button "First" in game/net/earshot.tscn
#: game/net/earshot.gd game/net/earshot.tscn
msgid "call"
msgstr "appeler"

#. A button: answer the call the other phone is making.
#. Button "Second" in game/net/earshot.tscn
#: game/net/earshot.gd game/net/earshot.tscn
msgid "answer"
msgstr "répondre"

#. A heading above a ring of marks: the other player is to be shown these
#. marks, and taps them in on their phone. "this" is the code.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "show this"
msgstr "montrer ceci"

#. Under the ring while the call is ringing. "answer" as in answering a phone
#. call.
#. Room: at most 1180 px in 17 px type; the English takes 178 px.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "waiting for an answer"
msgstr "en attente de réponse"

#. A button: hang up; stop calling.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "stop"
msgstr "arrêter"

#. A heading above a ring of twelve places: the player taps the four marks the
#. other player is showing, in order, to dial them.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "tap their code"
msgstr "entrez son code"

#. A button: undo the last tap of the code, one step back.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "back one"
msgstr "retour arrière"

#. A heading: the other player has picked up; the two phones are connected.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "answered"
msgstr "répondu"

#. A heading, when a call ends and the game has no more precise reason: nobody
#. picked up. The reason, in a sentence, is shown under it.
#. A heading of two to four words in large type, then one sentence that says
#. what to do, on a single line in 17 px type. Lowercase, plain words. The
#. "friend" owns a server that keeps the shared game world, "the water", and
#. sent the "invite" the player pasted.
#. A heading, and under it a sentence, shown on the screen of the phone that
#. dialled a four-mark code and got no answer. A "cell" is the player's
#. creature. The sentence is shown in 17 px type on one line: about 110
#. characters at most.
#. A heading and a sentence under it: nothing answered the code that was
#. tapped in. "Showing it" means the friend's phone is still displaying the
#. four marks.
#. entry: no_answer
#. Room: at most 1180 px in 17 px type; the English takes 86 px.
#: game/net/earshot.gd game/net/invite.gd game/net/net_session.gd
msgid "no answer"
msgstr "pas de réponse"

#. A button: try the same call again.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "again"
msgstr "réessayer"

#. A button: paste the invite from the clipboard. The invite is a one-line
#. message a friend sent you. Keep it short: the button is 264 px wide, in 20
#. px type.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "paste invite"
msgstr "coller l'invitation"

#. A button: paste a newer invite from the clipboard, to replace the one this
#. device keeps.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "paste new"
msgstr "coller une autre"

#. A button: leave this screen and go back.
#. The replay's last button: close the replay and go back to the game. The
#. same word is the pause screen's button that leaves the game. The replay's
#. button is the narrower: a long word runs into the speed button.
#. Button "Leave" in game/normal/normal_mode.tscn
#. Room: at most 64 px in 17 px type; the English takes 44 px.
#: game/net/earshot.gd game/normal/normal_mode.tscn game/replay/replay.gd
msgid "leave"
msgstr "quitter"

#. Under the ring while a call to a friend's server is ringing. A friend's
#. "water" is the pond (shared game world) their server keeps.
#. Room: at most 1180 px in 17 px type; the English takes 213 px.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "calling your friend's water"
msgstr "appel de l'eau de votre ami"

#. A question: delete the invite this device keeps?
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "forget this invite?"
msgstr "oublier cette invitation ?"

#. The consequence, under the question. It is a full sentence with a full
#. stop, unlike the lines around it.
#. Room: at most 1180 px in 17 px type; the English takes 450 px.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "you would need your friend's message to paste it back."
msgstr "vous auriez besoin du message de votre ami pour le coller à nouveau."

#. The safe answer to "delete pond water?" -- keep the world -- on a button
#. 208 px wide in 20 px type, beside "delete". The same word answers "forget
#. this invite?" on another screen.
#. Two buttons answering the question above: keep the invite, or forget it.
#. "keep" is the safe answer.
#. Room: at most 164 px in 20 px type; the English takes 47 px.
#: game/menu/corner.gd game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "keep"
msgstr "conserver"

#. A button: delete the invite this device keeps. It asks "forget this
#. invite?" first.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "forget"
msgstr "oublier"

#. Instruction, in 17 px type on one line. An invite is a one-line message a
#. friend sends you in a chat app: copy it there, then paste it into the game
#. with the button below.
#. Room: at most 1180 px in 17 px type; the English takes 446 px.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "copy the invite your friend sent you, then paste it here"
msgstr "copiez l'invitation que votre ami vous a envoyée, puis collez-la ici"

#. Under the heading when an invite is kept. A friend's "water" is the pond
#. (shared game world) their server keeps.
#. Room: at most 1180 px in 17 px type; the English takes 300 px.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "your friend's water, from their invite"
msgstr "l'eau de votre ami, depuis son invitation"

#. A full sentence in 17 px type: the friend's server refused this invite
#. earlier in this session. "paste a new one" means paste a newer invite,
#. which the friend must send.
#. Room: at most 1180 px in 17 px type; the English takes 501 px.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "your friend's server turned this invite away. paste a new one."
msgstr "le serveur de votre ami a rejeté cette invitation. collez-en une nouvelle."

#. Shown when the four marks tapped in do not form a valid code (a mistap).
#. The player is asked to tap the code in again.
#. Room: at most 1180 px in 17 px type; the English takes 248 px.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "that is not a code. tap it again."
msgstr "ce n'est pas un code. essayez à nouveau."

#. One word under the ring: the game is reaching out to the other phone now
#. that the whole code is in. Shown while it connects.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "reaching"
msgstr "connexion"

#. A small grey line: this device is not connected to any network, so it has
#. no address to show. Not a sentence; about 15 characters.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "no network here"
msgstr "pas de réseau"

#. The hint along the bottom edge, in 14 px type. It names the key that does
#. the thing, and the key differs by device: `back` is the Android Back button
#. or gesture, `esc` the Escape key, `ctrl+v` the paste shortcut. Translate
#. the verb ("leaves" = leaves this screen); key names may be written as they
#. are labelled on your keyboards.
#. The same hint, on every other page: the key leaves this screen.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "back leaves"
msgstr "retour pour quitter"

#. The hint along the bottom edge, in 14 px type. It names the key that does
#. the thing, and the key differs by device: `back` is the Android Back button
#. or gesture, `esc` the Escape key, `ctrl+v` the paste shortcut. Translate
#. the verb ("leaves" = leaves this screen); key names may be written as they
#. are labelled on your keyboards.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "ctrl+v pastes · esc leaves"
msgstr "ctrl+v pour coller · échap pour quitter"

#. The same hint, on the question "forget this invite?": the key goes back and
#. keeps the invite.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "back keeps it"
msgstr "retour pour conserver"

#. The same hint, on the question "forget this invite?": the key goes back and
#. keeps the invite.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "esc keeps it"
msgstr "échap pour conserver"

#. The same hint, on every other page: the key leaves this screen.
#. Label "Hint" in game/net/earshot.tscn
#: game/net/earshot.gd game/net/earshot.tscn
msgid "esc leaves"
msgstr "échap pour quitter"

#. A small grey line when a paste failed: the invite the device already kept
#. is still there. %s is that invite's address and port, as in "192.0.2.7 ·
#. 45772" -- keep %s as it is.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
#, c-format
msgid "still kept: %s"
msgstr "toujours conservé : %s"

#. The result of a paste: the invite on the clipboard is the one the device
#. already keeps. A short sentence under the heading.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "that invite is already kept"
msgstr "cette invitation est déjà conservée"

#. The result of a paste: the invite was read and saved on this device. Under
#. the heading, with its address and port below.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "invite kept"
msgstr "invitation conservée"

#. The result of a paste: a newer invite was read and replaced the one this
#. device kept.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "new invite kept"
msgstr "nouvelle invitation conservée"

#. The result of "forget": the invite was deleted from this device.
#: game/net/earshot.gd
msgid "invite forgotten"
msgstr "invitation oubliée"

#. What the game calls the way in to a friend's game far away, by an invite
#. the friend sent. It is the name of a button on the screen where a game is
#. started (320 px wide, 20 px type) and the heading of the screen behind it.
#. A short phrase: about 25 characters at most.
#. Room: at most 290 px in 20 px type; the English takes 83 px.
#: game/net/invite.gd
msgid "by invite"
msgstr "par invitation"

#. A heading of two to four words in large type, then one sentence that says
#. what to do, on a single line in 17 px type. Lowercase, plain words. The
#. "friend" owns a server that keeps the shared game world, "the water", and
#. sent the "invite" the player pasted.
#. entry: not_found
#. Room: at most 1180 px in 17 px type; the English takes 131 px.
#: game/net/invite.gd
msgid "no invite copied"
msgstr "aucune invitation copiée"

#. A heading of two to four words in large type, then one sentence that says
#. what to do, on a single line in 17 px type. Lowercase, plain words. The
#. "friend" owns a server that keeps the shared game world, "the water", and
#. sent the "invite" the player pasted.
#. entry: not_found
#. Room: at most 1180 px in 17 px type; the English takes 428 px.
#: game/net/invite.gd
msgid "copy your friend's whole message, then paste again."
msgstr "copiez le message complet de votre ami, puis collez à nouveau."

#. A heading of two to four words in large type, then one sentence that says
#. what to do, on a single line in 17 px type. Lowercase, plain words. The
#. "friend" owns a server that keeps the shared game world, "the water", and
#. sent the "invite" the player pasted.
#. entry: damaged
#. Room: at most 1180 px in 17 px type; the English takes 127 px.
#: game/net/invite.gd
msgid "invite damaged"
msgstr "invitation endommagée"

#. A heading of two to four words in large type, then one sentence that says
#. what to do, on a single line in 17 px type. Lowercase, plain words. The
#. "friend" owns a server that keeps the shared game world, "the water", and
#. sent the "invite" the player pasted.
#. entry: damaged
#. Room: at most 1180 px in 17 px type; the English takes 742 px.
#: game/net/invite.gd
msgid "some of it was lost or changed on the way. copy all of it, or ask your friend to send it again."
msgstr "une partie a été perdue ou modifiée. copiez-la en entier, ou demandez à votre ami de l'envoyer à nouveau."

#. A heading of two to four words in large type, then one sentence that says
#. what to do, on a single line in 17 px type. Lowercase, plain words. The
#. "friend" owns a server that keeps the shared game world, "the water", and
#. sent the "invite" the player pasted.
#. entry: unknown_version
#. Room: at most 1180 px in 17 px type; the English takes 153 px.
#: game/net/invite.gd
msgid "your game is older"
msgstr "votre jeu est trop ancien"

#. A heading of two to four words in large type, then one sentence that says
#. what to do, on a single line in 17 px type. Lowercase, plain words. The
#. "friend" owns a server that keeps the shared game world, "the water", and
#. sent the "invite" the player pasted.
#. entry: unknown_version
#. Room: at most 1180 px in 17 px type; the English takes 653 px.
#: game/net/invite.gd
msgid "this invite needs the update. take it from the launcher, restart, and paste again."
msgstr "cette invitation nécessite une mise à jour. prenez-la depuis le launcher, redémarrez, puis collez à nouveau."

#. A heading of two to four words in large type, then one sentence that says
#. what to do, on a single line in 17 px type. Lowercase, plain words. The
#. "friend" owns a server that keeps the shared game world, "the water", and
#. sent the "invite" the player pasted.
#. entry: not_kept
#. Room: at most 1180 px in 17 px type; the English takes 120 px.
#: game/net/invite.gd
msgid "invite not kept"
msgstr "invitation non conservée"

#. A heading of two to four words in large type, then one sentence that says
#. what to do, on a single line in 17 px type. Lowercase, plain words. The
#. "friend" owns a server that keeps the shared game world, "the water", and
#. sent the "invite" the player pasted.
#. entry: not_kept
#. Room: at most 1180 px in 17 px type; the English takes 617 px.
#: game/net/invite.gd
msgid "this device would not save the invite. free up some space, then paste again."
msgstr "cet appareil n'a pas pu sauvegarder l'invitation. libérez de l'espace, puis collez à nouveau."

#. A heading of two to four words in large type, then one sentence that says
#. what to do, on a single line in 17 px type. Lowercase, plain words. The
#. "friend" owns a server that keeps the shared game world, "the water", and
#. sent the "invite" the player pasted.
#. entry: no_invite
#. Room: at most 1180 px in 17 px type; the English takes 102 px.
#: game/net/invite.gd
msgid "no invite yet"
msgstr "aucune invitation"

#. A heading of two to four words in large type, then one sentence that says
