#. joined with a middle dot into a line of about 650 px; the longest English
#. line takes 540 px.
#: game/normal/gene_stats.gd
#, python-brace-format
msgid "level {} after {} strike"
msgid_plural "level {} after {} strikes"
msgstr[0] "niveau {} après {} impact"
msgstr[1] "niveau {} après {} impacts"

#. The odds line (14 px type) when the numbers switch is on: the copies of the
#. gene in words (see "one copy"), a middle dot, then whether a daughter cell
#. wears the gene. %s is "one copy", "two copies" or "three copies", already
#. translated: keep it first. About 50 characters at most.
#: game/normal/gene_stats.gd
#, c-format
msgid "%s · a daughter always wears it"
msgstr "%s · une cellule fille le porte toujours"

#. The same line when the chance is not certain. The first %s is the copies in
#. words, as above; the second is a percentage such as "55%", so the line
#. reads "one copy · 55% of daughters wear it". Keep both %s in this order.
#: game/normal/gene_stats.gd
#, c-format
msgid "%s · %s of daughters wear it"
msgstr "%s · %s des cellules filles le portent"

#. Two items added to the pause screen's caption when the numbers switch is
#. on: the cell's width, and its food tank in seconds, then how long the food
#. lasts while the cell just drifts ("a full tank: 36 s, 12 s drifting"). The
#. whole caption is a small line in 15 px type.
#. A phrase of a gene's numbers, in 14 px type; {} is a number the game
#. writes, so keep every {}, its unit (µm, s, ×, °) and its order. Phrases are
#. joined with a middle dot into a line of about 650 px; the longest English
#. line takes 540 px.
#: game/normal/gene_stats.gd
#, python-brace-format
msgid "{} µm across"
msgstr "{} µm de large"

#. Two items added to the pause screen's caption when the numbers switch is
#. on: the cell's width, and its food tank in seconds, then how long the food
#. lasts while the cell just drifts ("a full tank: 36 s, 12 s drifting"). The
#. whole caption is a small line in 15 px type.
#. A phrase of a gene's numbers, in 14 px type; {} is a number the game
#. writes, so keep every {}, its unit (µm, s, ×, °) and its order. Phrases are
#. joined with a middle dot into a line of about 650 px; the longest English
#. line takes 540 px.
#: game/normal/gene_stats.gd
#, python-brace-format
msgid "a full tank: {} s, {} s drifting"
msgstr "réservoir : {} s, {} s en dérive"

#. The name of an action the player's cell can be told to do by one of its
#. "instincts" (a rule the player writes: "when <a sense reports something> ->
#. <do this>"), on a small chip. Lowercase, a few short words. "hold still"
#. means: stop the tail (the flagellum, which swims) from beating, and keep it
#. still.
#. entry: flagellum.hold
#. Room: at most 112 px in 15 px type; the English takes 62 px.
#: game/normal/genome.gd
msgid "hold still"
msgstr "fige la queue"

#. Explains one action an "instinct" can make the cell do, on one line under
#. the instincts: its name (the same words as on its chip), a middle dot, then
#. what it does, lowercase. "Your tail" is the cell's flagellum, which swims;
#. "two copies" means the gene is carried twice in the cell's DNA, which is
#. what lets the tail be held still. "For free" means it costs no food.
#. entry: flagellum.hold
#. Room: at most 856 px in 15 px type; the English takes 615 px.
#: game/normal/genome.gd
msgid "hold still · hold your tail still and keep steering, for free. needs two copies of your tail."
msgstr "fige la queue · immobiliser la queue et continuer à se diriger, gratuitement. demande deux copies de la queue."

#. Said of an "instinct" (a rule the player wrote) that cannot act yet,
#. because the action it uses needs a gene carried twice. "Asleep" is the
#. state's name; "two copies of your tail" means the tail gene (the flagellum)
#. carried twice in the cell's DNA. Lowercase.
#. entry: flagellum.hold
#. Room: at most 856 px in 14 px type; the English takes 245 px.
#: game/normal/genome.gd
msgid "asleep: needs two copies of your tail"
msgstr "endormi : demande deux copies de la queue"

#. Said when the player picks an action their cell cannot do yet, because it
#. needs a gene carried twice. "hold still" is the action's name, as on its
#. chip; "two copies of your tail" means the tail gene (the flagellum) carried
#. twice in the cell's DNA. Lowercase.
#. entry: flagellum.hold
#. Room: at most 856 px in 14 px type; the English takes 255 px.
#: game/normal/genome.gd
msgid "hold still needs two copies of your tail"
msgstr "« fige la queue » demande deux copies de la queue"

#. A hint in 18 px type over the water, the first time the player's cell
#. divides in two. The two daughters are on screen, one each side, and the
#. player chooses which one to carry on as by leaning toward it (a drag on a
#. phone, the A and D keys on a keyboard). "Them" is the two daughters.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "lean into one of them"
msgstr "penchez-vous vers l'une d'elles"

#. The pause screen's "camera" button, which flips between two ways of drawing
#. the water. `north up`: the world stays still and the cell turns in it.
#. `forward up`: the world turns round the cell, so the way the cell is facing
#. is always up the screen. Keep each to about 12 characters: the button sizes
#. to its text and the whole left column grows with it.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "forward up"
msgstr "avant en haut"

#. The pause screen's "camera" button, which flips between two ways of drawing
#. the water. `north up`: the world stays still and the cell turns in it.
#. `forward up`: the world turns round the cell, so the way the cell is facing
#. is always up the screen. Keep each to about 12 characters: the button sizes
#. to its text and the whole left column grows with it.
#. Button "Toggle" in game/normal/normal_mode.tscn
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd game/normal/normal_mode.tscn
msgid "north up"
msgstr "nord en haut"

#. The pause screen's "controls" button, which cycles through three ways of
#. steering with a thumb. `anywhere`: drag anywhere on the water, nothing is
#. drawn. `stick`: a drawn joystick in one corner. `pads`: drawn buttons in
#. the corners. One lowercase word each, about 10 characters at most: the
#. button sizes to its text and the whole left column grows with it.
#. Button "Toggle" in game/normal/normal_mode.tscn
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd game/normal/normal_mode.tscn
msgid "anywhere"
msgstr "partout"

#. The pause screen's "controls" button, which cycles through three ways of
#. steering with a thumb. `anywhere`: drag anywhere on the water, nothing is
#. drawn. `stick`: a drawn joystick in one corner. `pads`: drawn buttons in
#. the corners. One lowercase word each, about 10 characters at most: the
#. button sizes to its text and the whole left column grows with it.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "stick"
msgstr "joystick"

#. The pause screen's "controls" button, which cycles through three ways of
#. steering with a thumb. `anywhere`: drag anywhere on the water, nothing is
#. drawn. `stick`: a drawn joystick in one corner. `pads`: drawn buttons in
#. the corners. One lowercase word each, about 10 characters at most: the
#. button sizes to its text and the whole left column grows with it.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "pads"
msgstr "boutons"

#. The first line a new player sees, in 18 px type over the water, teaching
#. how to steer: on a phone, drag a finger; on a keyboard, hold the A key to
#. turn one way and the D key to turn the other. Keep the key letters A and D.
#. One short line: about 25 characters.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "drag to turn"
msgstr "glissez pour tourner"

#. The first line a new player sees, in 18 px type over the water, teaching
#. how to steer: on a phone, drag a finger; on a keyboard, hold the A key to
#. turn one way and the D key to turn the other. Keep the key letters A and D.
#. One short line: about 25 characters.
#. Label "Onboarding" in game/normal/normal_mode.tscn
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd game/normal/normal_mode.tscn
msgid "A · D to turn"
msgstr "A · D pour tourner"

#. A notice in 18 px type, for seven seconds, when the cell has grown a new
#. sense (a gene waiting for a place on its body). "Place it" means choose
#. where on the body the new organ grows. On a phone the player holds their
#. finger on their own cell; on a keyboard they hold the E key: keep the
#. letter e. About 45 characters at most.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "a sense grew · hold your body to place it"
msgstr "un sens a grandi · maintenez votre corps pour le placer"

#. A notice in 18 px type, for seven seconds, when the cell has grown a new
#. sense (a gene waiting for a place on its body). "Place it" means choose
#. where on the body the new organ grows. On a phone the player holds their
#. finger on their own cell; on a keyboard they hold the E key: keep the
#. letter e. About 45 characters at most.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "a sense grew · hold e to place it"
msgstr "un sens a grandi · maintenez E pour le placer"

#. A small caption, in 15 px type, beside the row of genes that are waiting
#. for a place on the body: genes the cell has just eaten and not yet placed.
#. One lowercase word. Four chips fit on a row beside it; a wider word makes
#. the fourth wrap onto the next row.
#. Room: at most 64 px in 15 px type; the English takes 54 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "waiting"
msgstr "attente"

#. The hint under the figure, in 14 px type, about the gene being read: how
#. many copies of it the cell's DNA holds (one to three) and so how likely a
#. daughter cell is to wear it (to show it as an organ). The copies are words,
#. not digits, on purpose. At most about 50 characters: the row is 560 px wide
#. and shares it with a level and a gauge.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "one copy · a daughter may not wear it"
msgstr "une copie · une cellule fille peut ne pas le porter"

#. The hint under the figure, in 14 px type, about the gene being read: how
#. many copies of it the cell's DNA holds (one to three) and so how likely a
#. daughter cell is to wear it (to show it as an organ). The copies are words,
#. not digits, on purpose. At most about 50 characters: the row is 560 px wide
#. and shares it with a level and a gauge.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "two copies · a daughter probably wears it"
msgstr "deux copies · une cellule fille le porte probablement"

#. The hint under the figure, in 14 px type, about the gene being read: how
#. many copies of it the cell's DNA holds (one to three) and so how likely a
#. daughter cell is to wear it (to show it as an organ). The copies are words,
#. not digits, on purpose. At most about 50 characters: the row is 560 px wide
#. and shares it with a level and a gauge.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "three copies · a daughter always wears it"
msgstr "trois copies · une cellule fille le porte toujours"

#. The hint (see the copies line above) for the mouth gene, which every
#. daughter always wears. At most about 50 characters.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "the mouth · a daughter always wears it"
msgstr "la bouche · une cellule fille le porte toujours"

#. The hint under an empty place on the body: nothing is there, so nothing can
#. be passed on to a daughter from it. At most about 50 characters.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "an empty slot · nothing to pass on from here"
msgstr "un emplacement vide · rien à transmettre depuis ici"

#. The hint while the player is about to write a waiting gene over one that is
#. already in the DNA. %s is the short word of the gene that would be lost
#. (such as `eat` or `ping`): keep %s as it is. "Your body keeps it" means
#. this cell keeps the organ for the rest of its life, though its daughters
#. will not inherit it. At most about 55 characters with a word in place of
#. %s.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "%s leaves your dna · your body keeps it"
msgstr "%s quitte votre ADN · votre corps le garde"

#. The same hint for a gene the DNA carries but the body does not wear, so
#. there is no second half. %s is the gene's short word.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "%s leaves your dna"
msgstr "%s quitte votre ADN"

#. As the hint above, for a gene that has a level (it grows with use). The
#. first %s is the gene's short word, the %d the level. Keep both, in this
#. order. 355 px at most, in 14 px type: about 55 characters.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "%s leaves your dna · level %d ends with this body"
msgstr "%s quitte votre ADN · ce corps garde le niveau %d"

#. Same, for a levelled gene the body does not wear. %s is the gene's short
#. word, %d the level.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "%s leaves your dna · its level %d is lost"
msgstr "%s quitte votre ADN · son niveau %d est perdu"

#. A gene's level, a whole number that grows with use: "level 7". Keep %d.
#. Shown in 14 px type at the start of the hint row.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "level %d"
msgstr "niveau %d"

#. All the `ACT_` lines are one line of instructions in 14 px type, centred
#. under the figure, telling the player what the next tap or release will do.
#. A "slot" is one of seven places round the cell's body where a gene sits;
#. "place" a gene means put it in a slot; "your daughters may wear it" means
#. the cells this one divides into may show the gene as an organ. About 50
#. characters at most (the row is 560 px wide). This one: a gene is waiting,
#. none is chosen.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "tap a slot · your daughters may wear it"
msgstr "appuyez sur un emplacement · vos cellules filles peuvent le porter"

#. A slot is chosen for the waiting gene; a second tap confirms.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "tap again to place"
msgstr "appuyez à nouveau pour placer"

#. The two %s are the short words of two genes, such as `eat` and `ping`: the
#. first is the waiting gene, the second the gene it would replace in the DNA.
#. Keep both %s, in this order.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "tap again to write %s over %s"
msgstr "appuyez à nouveau pour écrire %s sur %s"

#. While the player drags a waiting gene over an empty slot; letting go places
#. it there. %s is the gene's short word, such as `eat`.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "let go to place %s here"
msgstr "lâchez pour placer %s ici"

#. While dragging a waiting gene over a slot that already holds a gene:
#. letting go only selects it, and a second tap writes over it. The two %s are
#. short gene words: the one being dragged, then the one it would replace.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "let go, then tap again to place %s over %s"
msgstr "lâchez, puis appuyez à nouveau pour placer %s sur %s"

#. Under a gene that is already in a slot: it can be dragged to another slot.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "drag it to another slot"
msgstr "glissez-le vers un autre emplacement"

#. While dragging a gene that is not over any slot. %s is its short word, such
#. as `eat`; "put it there" means into a slot.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "%s · let go over a slot to put it there"
msgstr "%s · lâchez sur un emplacement pour l'y mettre"

#. While dragging a gene over an empty slot of the body. %s is its short word.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "let go to move %s here"
msgstr "lâchez pour déplacer %s ici"

#. While dragging a gene over a slot that holds another: letting go swaps
#. them. The two %s are the two genes' short words.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "let go to swap %s and %s"
msgstr "lâchez pour échanger %s et %s"

#. While dragging a gene back over the slot it came from: letting go cancels
#. the move. %s is the gene's short word.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "let go to leave %s where it is"
msgstr "lâchez pour laisser %s où il est"

#. For a gene that can grow in two different ways (the player picks one, for
#. good). %s is the gene's short word, such as `beam`.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "tap again to choose how %s grows"
msgstr "appuyez à nouveau pour choisir comment %s grandit"

#. The word for a toxin gene that has been eaten and is waiting to be placed,
#. on its chip in the tray and on a finger dragging it. Placed outside the
#. body it becomes `venom`, inside it becomes `poison`; until then it is
#. neither. One short lowercase word, like the other gene words.
#. Room: at most 47 px in 13 px type; the English takes 33 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "toxin"
msgstr "toxine"

#. The gene line for a toxin that is waiting, before a slot is chosen: it
#. hurts over time, and becomes venom or poison depending on where it is
#. placed. After the gene's scientific name and a middle dot. No longer than
#. the English.
#. Room: at most 440 px in 15 px type; the English takes 371 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "a toxin that goes on hurting, as venom or as poison"
msgstr "une toxine qui fait mal longtemps, en venin ou en poison"

#. The line for the empty slot inside the body (the one slot in the middle of
#. the body, not round it): nothing is there yet, and a toxin placed there
#. becomes poison.
#. Room: at most 520 px in 15 px type; the English takes 350 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "nothing inside yet · a toxin here becomes poison"
msgstr "rien dedans pour l'instant · une toxine ici devient du poison"

#. Under that line, for the empty inside slot: the slot is inside the cell's
#. body, and a toxin is the only gene that can go there.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type; the English takes 272 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "inside your body · only a toxin goes here"
msgstr "dans votre corps · seule une toxine va ici"

#. While a toxin is waiting and no slot is chosen: tapping a slot round the
#. body (outside) makes it venom, the slot in the body (inside) makes it
#. poison.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type; the English takes 271 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "tap a slot · venom outside, poison inside"
msgstr "appuyez sur un emplacement · venin dehors, poison dedans"

#. When the player tries to put a gene other than a toxin into the slot inside
#. the body: only a toxin works there. %s is the gene's short word, such as
#. `swim`.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word in
#. place of the placeholders; the English takes 178 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "%s works only outside"
msgstr "%s ne fonctionne que dehors"

#. A slot is chosen for a waiting toxin; a second tap places it, as the form
#. it takes in that slot. %s is `venom` or `poison`.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word in
#. place of the placeholders; the English takes 205 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "tap again to place %s here"
msgstr "appuyez à nouveau pour placer %s ici"

#. A slot is chosen for a waiting toxin, but the toxin would become a form the
#. cell already carries, so a second tap adds one copy of it where it already
#. is. %s is `venom` or `poison`.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word in
#. place of the placeholders; the English takes 225 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "tap again to add a copy to %s"
msgstr "appuyez à nouveau : %s gagne une copie"

#. As above, but that form already has the most copies a gene can have, three,
#. so placing it there would do nothing. %s is `venom` or `poison`.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word in
#. place of the placeholders; the English takes 215 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "%s has three copies already"
msgstr "%s a déjà trois copies"

#. While dragging a waiting toxin over a slot where it would add a copy to a
#. form the cell already carries: letting go chooses the slot, and a second
#. tap adds the copy. %s is `venom` or `poison`.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word in
#. place of the placeholders; the English takes 305 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "let go, then tap again to add a copy to %s"
msgstr "lâchez, puis appuyez à nouveau : %s gagne une copie"

#. While dragging a gene to a slot where it would turn into a form the cell
#. already carries (venom outside, poison inside), which is not allowed. %s is
#. `venom` or `poison`.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word in
#. place of the placeholders; the English takes 366 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "here it would become %s, which you already carry"
msgstr "ici il deviendrait %s, que vous portez déjà"

#. While dragging a toxin into a slot of the other place: letting go moves it
#. there, and it changes form. The first %s is its word now, the second the
#. word it becomes, such as "let go to move venom here · it becomes poison".
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word and
#. your second widest in place of the placeholders; the English takes 315 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "let go to move %s here · it becomes %s"
msgstr "lâchez pour déplacer %s ici · il y devient %s"

#. While dragging a gene onto another, where the swap moves one of them
#. between outside and inside and changes its form. The first two %s are the
#. two genes' words; the last two say which one changes and what it becomes.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word,
#. your second widest, your second widest and your second widest in place of
#. the placeholders; the English takes 382 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "let go to swap %s and %s · %s becomes %s"
msgstr "lâchez pour échanger %s et %s · %s devient %s"

#. While dragging venom onto poison (or the reverse): the two swap places and
#. change forms, so in effect they trade copies. The two %s are the two words.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word and
#. your second widest in place of the placeholders; the English takes 351 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "let go to swap %s and %s · they trade copies"
msgstr "lâchez pour échanger %s et %s · ils échangent leurs copies"

#. A world's name until the player types one: a real place a microscopist
#. takes a water sample from ("pond water"). A "world" is one of the three the
#. player keeps: a drop of water and everything living in it. Short and
#. lowercase, as a player would name it; at most 20 characters, as a typed
#. name is. Shown in the top-right corner after the word "world", in 17 px
#. type, and in the "your worlds" menu, in 20 px type.
#. Room: at most 220 px in 20 px type; the English takes 112 px.
#: game/normal/drops.gd
msgid "pond water"
msgstr "eau de mare"

#. A world's name until the player types one: a real place a microscopist
#. takes a water sample from ("pond water"). A "world" is one of the three the
#. player keeps: a drop of water and everything living in it. Short and
#. lowercase, as a player would name it; at most 20 characters, as a typed
